# verify/Dockerfile.dockerignore — BuildKit's PER-DOCKERFILE ignore file
# (`<dockerfile>.dockerignore` wins over the context-root `.dockerignore`).
#
# The build context is the REPOSITORY ROOT, because verify/Dockerfile copies
# robot_sw/src and robot_sw/constraints-detector.txt. Everything else in this repo is
# either read from the read-only checkout at run time (sim/, robot_sw/models/) or has
# nothing to do with verification at all (web/) — sending it would only make the context
# bigger and the layer cache more fragile.
#
# ⚠ PATTERNS NEED `**/` (measured on robot_sw/.dockerignore, 2026-09-01): a
# .dockerignore is NOT a .gitignore — `__pycache__/` matches only the CONTEXT ROOT's
# directory, so it would leave src/go2_detector/go2_detector/__pycache__ in place and a
# stale .pyc would shadow a source file inside the image.

# Not part of the verification image.
web/
compose.yaml
README.md
cv-infra-contract-update-proposal.md

# Run-time inputs, read from the checkout mount — never baked (see verify/Dockerfile).
sim/
robot_sw/models/

# Case output. The directory is committed (verify/out/.gitkeep); its contents are run
# residue and would invalidate the context hash on every local run.
verify/out/

# Repository metadata and developer working-tree noise.
.git/
.github/
.env
.env.example
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/*.egg-info
**/build
**/install
**/log
.ruff_cache/
